    {
      "question": "q-82178",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "f6e0d45c74c47387102e54584f2cd326d0450532c1b400babe8f982017577782",
      "new_sha256": "3a07e1c4adea0923b93092c89b0fe6b0c42b781ff4ae4903bc116e3e3794ef09",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "q-82178",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-{90}^{\u2218}\\le \\theta \\le {90}^{\u2218}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's take a look at the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14035417/assets/d93c490adbb5cdbc0e9a09b60eea9b82ab93be8e871e334423abc17ddd62955e.png)\n\nFrom the values on the unit circle, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061({315}^{\u2218})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nHowever, ${315}^{\u2218}$ does not lie within the range of $\\theta .$ To get an angle that's coterminal with ${315}^{\u2218}$ that lies within the range of $\\theta ,$ we subtract ${360}^{\u2218}.$\n\n$$\n{315}^{\u2218}-{360}^{\u2218}=-{45}^{\u2218}.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=-{45}^{\u2218}.\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14035417/state.json",
          "file_sha256": "9680257bbfd9cb8e41823111f00ab857ea9132a14d813c4ce3b817cbe66d0e99"
        }
      ],
